---
# Drops the 403s the bouncer itself returns before they reach any scenario.
# Otherwise a banned client that keeps retrying trips http-generic-403-bf and
# renews its own ban for as long as it retries.
#
# A request rejected by a middleware has no ServiceAddr in the access log. 403s
# from an application always carry one, so they still count. AppSec blocks are
# dropped here too, but they raise alerts through their own 'appsec' acquisition.
name: local/whitelist-bouncer-rejections
description: "Ignore 403s generated by the Traefik bouncer rather than an application"
whitelist:
  reason: "403 generated by the bouncer, not an application"
  expression:
    - "evt.Meta.log_type == 'http_access-log' && evt.Meta.http_status == '403' && evt.Unmarshaled.traefik.ServiceAddr == nil"
